<h1>Essay Thesis Strength Dataset</h1>

<br>

<p>This page is a distribution site of essay data for the task of Essay Thesis Strength. Data available on this page include annotated Thesis Strength scores as well as attributes the thesis statement
that impact a thesis’s strength. This annotation is composed of 1021 essays randomly chosen from the ICLE corpus (<a href="https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Sylviane_Granger/publication/288182446_International_Corpus_of_Learner_English_Version_2_Handbook_and_CD-ROM/links/567eeecc08ae1e63f1e7f259/International-Corpus-of-Learner-English-Version-2-Handbook-and-CD-ROM.pdf">Granger et al. 2009</a>)</p>


<p>The problem of <i>Essay Thesis Strength</i> for which this dataset is intended is described in:</p>

<ul> <li> Zixuan Ke, Hrishikesh Inamdar, Hui Lin and <a
href="http://www.hlt.utdallas.edu/~vince/">Vincent Ng</a>, <a
href="http://www.hlt.utdallas.edu/~zixuan/EssayScoring/ThesisStrength/ACL2019.pdf">Give Me More Feedback II: Annotating Thesis Strength and Related Attributes in Student Essays</a>,
<i>Proceedings of the 57th Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics (Volume 1: Long Papers), 2019. </i> 
</ul> 

